ena","address":{"city":"Tampa","state":"FL","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1396.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":19092,"officials":[{"fullName":"Francois St. Laurent","displayName":"Francois St. Laurent","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Libor Suchanek","displayName":"Libor Suchanek","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Corey Syvret","displayName":"Corey Syvret","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Ryan Jackson","displayName":"Ryan Jackson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Ilya Mikheyev scores twice and Lightning beat the Blackhawks 4-1 to improve to 8-0 at home","description":"— Ilya Mikheyev scored twice to back Andrei Vasilevskiy and the Tampa Bay Lightning beat the Chicago Blackhawks 4-1 on Thursday night to remain perfect at home this season.","story":"TAMPA, Fla. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4422415/ilya-mikheyev\">Ilya Mikheyev</a> scored twice to back <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976847/andrei-vasilevskiy\">Andrei Vasilevskiy</a> and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tb/tampa-bay-lightning\">Tampa Bay Lightning</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-blackhawks\">Chicago Blackhawks</a> 4-1 on Thursday night to remain perfect at home this season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5157/victor-hedman\">Victor Hedman</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4954/ryan-mcdonagh\">Ryan McDonagh</a> also scored. Vasilevskiy made 24 saves, allowing only <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149231/roman-kantserov\">Roman Kantserov</a>'s goal with 49 seconds left.\n\n\r\n              The Lightning are 8-0-0 at home and 10-3-2 overall, while the Blackhawks are 0-7-1 on the road and 4-12-1 overall.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4894729/arvid-soderblom\">Arvid Soderblom</a> stopped 31 shots for Chicago.\n\n\r\n              Hedman opened the scoring on a power play at 4:12 of the first period. The defenseman has four goals this season.\n\n\r\n              Mikheyev connected with 1:38 in the opening period.\n\n\r\n              McDonagh scored on a slap shot at 2:38 of the third, and Mikheyev added his second of the game and fourth of the season on a tip at 5:07.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blackhawks: At Carolina on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              Lightning: At Minnesota on Saturday night to open four-game trip.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-06T02:56:34Z"}}